# Build-context filter. The Dockerfile's `COPY . .` sends whatever survives this file into the
# image build, so it decides what can reach `next build`.
#
# DELIBERATELY ABSENT: any exception that lets a `.env` file into the context. Nothing in .env*
# may ever enter an image — Next would load it during `next build` and inline its NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# values over the ARGs. Build-time values arrive as ARGs from Railway (see the Dockerfile).

# ---- never in the image ----
node_modules
.next
out
.git
.github
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.DS_Store
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
coverage

# ---- secrets. No exception line may follow this block. ----
.env
.env.*

# ---- docs and deploy config: read by humans and Railway, never by `next build` ----
*.md
*.mdx
*.markdown
Dockerfile
railway.json
